HealthySystems (HLTSYS) founded in 2013 is a spin-off company from University of Porto who focuses on data integration and data Interoperability, cybersecurity, security technologies, security auditing, performance consulting and data protection laws from its customers. Our co-founders and collaborators have various scientific publications in international journals, congresses and book chapters.They are responsible for curricular units and courses on security and their visibility leads them to be periodically invited as speakers in national and international lectures and events, and has already given some lectures, by invitation, at events organized by the National Commission for the Data Protection (CNPD). Some other members of our team additionally integrate and collaborate with the national standards body (health informatics group IPQ - CT199) and are current PhD fellows in the health area.
Our products and services include the optimization of systems interoperability and integrations auditing, cybersecurity systems, and the development of security information systems, network infrastructure optimization, and performance audits as well advice on data protection laws. Verification of data quality in databases and real-time message exchange technologies - Interoperability. We are experienced in the study, implementation and evaluation of cybersecurity and interoperability in healthcare and other industry sectors. HLTSYS has a team of integrative professionals with vast national and international experience, in all needs related to the implementation of integrations between information systems in health institutions. 
The Company's growth has been sustained both in terms of revenue and in terms of human resources. All employees have higher education with extensive experience in R&D, highlighting the existence of specialized and certified technical staff: 

 - Mirth Corp (Quality Systems, Inc), which enables us to assist our customers in the choice, acquisition, parameterization and maintenance of highly available Mirth server clusters capable of meeting the most demanding interoperability challenges (HL7 in particular);
 - ISO/IEC 27001 Lead Implementor Standard. Produced to provide a model that allows to establish, implement, operate, monitor, analyse critically, maintain and improve an Information Security Management System;
 - ITIL&reg; 2011 Foundations in IT Management. Through ITIL structure we obtain a set of recommended practices for IT services management (ITSM), which focuses in the alignment of IT services with business needs;
 - HL7 Portuguese Affiliate Chapter, which has as main goal stimulate the global interoperability in Portugal, in the health sector, through the development of standards and mobilizing its adoption and implementation in the sector.
Our products are the result of innovative Research and Technological Development projects carried out by our team, whose knowledge and experience were at the origin of its conceptualization. Over the last few years HealthySystems has been developing and maintaining a solid set of relationships with Scientific and Technological entities, of the public, private and associative business sectors, whose relationships also contributed to our solutions. HealthySystems has developed several research projects in security and interoperability areas. These projects allowed several national and international awards. The relevance of developed R&D activities led to the creation of an R&D core in HLTSYS in 2015, whose projects have been certified by ANI, IAPMEI and FCT under the System and Tax Incentives for Entreprise R&D. Therefore, HealthySystems plans to continue to grow, sustainable and innovative way.

Eyecon Software is a firm that provides relevant data and software solutions customized to address optimal performance and savings' opportunities to businesses across varied industries.
Eyecon Software provides innovative solutions that combine the latest technologies such as wireless sensors, satellite data, image recognition and artificial intelligence to provide greater visibility and efficiency in all aspects of your business. Eyecon solutions make it possible to interconnect equipment, people and services to get a clear picture of the operating state of the business ecosystem and to offer visible competitive advantages such as:
Continuous Monitoring - Real-time monitoring of assets;
Remote Control - management of assets through actuators;
Dashboards by Measurement - Construction of customized monitoring panels;
Predictive Maintenance - Use of data analysis techniques to identify patterns of activity and detect future problems;
Alarms - Management and configuration of alarms;

Reports - Creation of detailed activity reports.
